title: Checkout relaunch
description: One board for the whole project: the system as it is, and canvases inside it for discovery, the plan, the data and the numbers. Every feature of diagram is used somewhere here.
direction: right
routing: orthogonal
theme: brand

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the system
# shapes, colours, details, tags, links, sections, every kind of arrow

customer: Customer [person]
support: Support team [person, teal]
stripe: Stripe [cloud, purple, detail: payments, link: https://docs.stripe.com/payments]
mail: E-mail provider [cloud]
note: Every write carries an\nidempotency key [sticky, link: #orders]
legacy: Legacy cart [document, gray, detail: retired in Q1, tags: legacy deprecated]
ledger: Ledger export [parallelogram]
status: All systems normal [text, green]

group edge: Edge [gray] {
  web: Storefront [rounded, detail: Next.js, tags: frontend]
  gateway: API gateway [hexagon]
}
group backend: Backend [blue] {
  orders: Orders API [detail: Rust · Axum, tags: core]
  group pay: Payments [purple] {
    payments: Payments [detail: Rust, link: #payments-flow-link]
    fraud: Fraud score > 80? [diamond, orange]
  }
  group async: Async [teal] {
    queue: Job queue [pill]
    worker: Fulfilment worker
  }
  db: Postgres [cylinder]
  cache: Redis [cylinder, #d1495b]
}

customer -> web: browses
web -> gateway: HTTPS [thick]
gateway -> orders: POST /orders
orders -> payments: charge
payments -> fraud
fraud -> stripe: no
fraud -> support: yes [red]
orders -> db, cache
orders ..> queue: order.created
queue ..> worker
worker -> mail: receipt
worker => ledger: nightly
legacy -- orders: replaced by [dotted]
cache <-> db: warm-up [dashed]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the way into the canvases
# a box with `canvas:` opens a board inside this one; its shape is how the link looks

group inside: Inside this board [gray] {
  discovery-link: Discovery [pill, blue, canvas: discovery]
  plan-link: Delivery plan [canvas: plan, detail: gantt · kanban · risks · decisions]
  data-link: Data & flows [text, canvas: data]
  metrics-link: Metrics [sticky, yellow, canvas: metrics]
  payments-flow-link: Payments, step by step [rounded, purple, canvas: data]
}

discovery-link -> plan-link -> data-link

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- review
comment on payments by deyan: Should payments own its own database?
reply c1 by ana: Not before launch; a separate schema is enough.
comment on queue->worker by ana: What happens when the worker crashes mid-order?
comment c3 at 40,-60 by deyan: Add the admin dashboard to this picture
comment on legacy by sam: Can we delete it now? [resolved, resolution: "Removed from the menu; code goes in Q1"]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- a theme of our own
theme brand {
  font: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif
  radius: 10
  blue: #3b6fd8
  light {
    background: #f7f8fa
    section: #eef2f8
  }
  dark {
    background: #0f1318
    section: #161c24
  }
}

# ================================================================ canvases

canvas discovery: Discovery {
  # what we learned, and the task for the coding agent, as a prompt mindmap
  direction: right

  quote: "I type my card in every single time" — interview #4 [sticky, yellow]
  screen: Today's checkout [image: wire, w: 248, h: 178]
  tickets: 38% of support tickets are about cards [text, red]

  mindmap task: Add saved payment methods to checkout [layout: both] {
    Context
      Rails monolith, Stripe already integrated
      Checkout is one page: app/views/checkout
      Customers re-enter cards on every order [link: #quote]
    Goal
      Returning customers pay in one click
      Cards stored by Stripe, never by us
    Constraints [red]
      No new services
      PCI scope must not grow
      Feature flag: saved_cards
    Steps
      Model: customer has many payment methods
      Stripe SetupIntent on first payment
      Picker on the checkout page
    Acceptance [green]
      Second order needs no card details
      Flag off: checkout unchanged
    Open questions [collapsed]
      Default card per customer?
      What about expired cards?
  }

  mindmap retro: Sprint 42 retro [layout: down] {
    Went well [green]
      Shipped the importer a week early
      Pairing on the parser
    Didn't [red]
      Flaky CI on macOS runners
    Try next [blue]
      Async stand-ups
  }

  quote ..> customers-re-enter-cards-on-every-order

  comment on quote by ana: Same in interviews #2 and #7

  canvas interviews: Interview notes {
    layout: grid

    i1: Shops weekly, always re-enters the card [sticky, green]
    i2: Gave up when 3-D Secure timed out [sticky, red]
    i3: Wants Apple Pay more than saved cards [sticky, blue]
    i4: Didn't notice the guest checkout [sticky]
  }

  interviews-link: All interview notes [box, canvas: interviews]

  asset wire: data:image/png;base64,
}

canvas plan: Delivery plan {
  # when, who does what, what could go wrong, and why we chose what we chose

  gantt launch: Launch plan [start: 2026-10-12, scale: week] {
    Design [5d, owner: mia, done]
    Build [2w, after: design, owner: sam, done: 40%]
    Docs [3d, after: design, purple]
    Beta [1w, after: build, orange]
    Launch day [after: beta docs, milestone, green]
  }

  gantt marketing: Marketing [start: 2026-10-19, scale: week] {
    Landing page [1w]
    Announcement [after: launch/launch-day, milestone]
  }

  kanban sprint: Sprint 12 {
    column todo: To do {
      saved: Saved cards [owner: ana]
      a11y: Accessibility pass [detail: forms and focus order]
    }
    column doing: Doing {
      onepage: One-page checkout [blue, owner: sam, link: #build]
    }
    column review: In review {
      emails: Order emails
    }
    column done: Done {
      intent: Payment intents [green]
    }
  }

  risks delivery: Delivery risks {
    Stripe review slips [p: 4, i: 4, owner: ana, detail: "Their review takes up to 4 weeks"]
    3-D Secure timeouts [p: 3, i: 4]
    Scope creep [p: 2, i: 3]
    Key engineer leaves [p: 1, i: 5, owner: deyan]
    Unknown unknowns
  }

  adr psp: Use one payment provider [accepted] {
    context: Two providers double the integration and reconciliation work.
    options: Stripe only; Stripe + Adyen
    decision: Stripe only, with payment intents.
    consequences: A Stripe outage stops checkout; we keep a status page.
  }

  adr wallets: Add Apple Pay first [proposed] {
    context: Interviews ask for wallets more than saved cards.
    decision: Ship Apple Pay before saved cards.
  }

  adr cart: Keep the legacy cart [superseded] {
    decision: Run both carts side by side.
  }

  table raci: Who does what {
    task      | lead | PM | VP Eng
    Discovery | R    | A  | I
    Spec      | A    | R  | C
    Release   | R    | C  | A [green]
  }

  table options: Hosting options {
    option | cost          | latency | notes
    Local  | $0            | 40 ms   | Needs an 8B model on every laptop
    Hosted | $1.2k / month | 300 ms  | Data leaves the laptop [red]
  }

  wallets -> cart: supersedes

  comment on beta by mia: Do we need a second week?
}

canvas data: Data & flows {
  # the data model as an ER diagram, the payment as a sequence, order-to-cash in swimlanes

  entity teams: Teams {
    id:         uuid [pk]
    name:       text [unique]
    created_at: timestamptz [default: now()]
  }
  entity customers: Customers {
    id:         uuid [pk]
    team_id:    uuid [fk: teams, rel: belongs to]
    email:      citext [unique]
    bio:        text [null]
  }
  entity cards: Saved cards {
    id:          uuid [pk]
    customer_id: uuid [fk: customers, rel: owned by]
    stripe_pm:   text [unique]
  }
  entity profiles: Profiles {
    customer_id [pk, fk: customers]
    nickname
  }

  sequence pay: Pay for an order {
    shopper: Shopper [person]
    page: Checkout page
    api: Orders API
    psp: Stripe [cloud]
    shopper -> page: Pay €42
    page -> api: POST /orders/42/pay
    api -> psp: create payment intent
    psp ..> api: client secret
    api ..> page: client secret
    page -> psp: confirm card (3-D Secure)
    psp -> api: webhook payment.succeeded
    api -> api: mark order paid
    page ..> shopper: Thank you page
  }

  lanes order: Order to cash {
    lane buyer: Customer {
      place: Place order [pill, green]
      paid: Pay invoice
    }
    lane sales: Sales {
      check: Credit OK? [diamond]
      confirm: Confirm order
    }
    lane finance: Finance [blue] {
      invoice: Send invoice
      book: Book payment [pill]
    }
  }

  crm: CRM [cylinder]

  place -> check
  check -> confirm: yes
  check -> place: no
  confirm -> invoice -> paid -> book
  confirm ..> crm

  comment on check: Who sets the credit limit?
}

canvas metrics: Metrics {
  layout: grid
  theme: paper

  chart revenue: Revenue by quarter [bar, unit: k€] {
    quarter | EU  | US
    Q1      | 120 | 80
    Q2      | 150 | 95
    Q3      | 170 | 130
    Q4      | 160 | 150
  }

  chart stacked: Revenue, stacked [bar, stacked, unit: k€] {
    quarter | EU  | US
    Q1      | 120 | 80
    Q2      | 150 | 95
    Q3      | 170 | 130
  }

  chart ttv: Time to pay [bar, horizontal, unit: s] {
    Guest checkout 74
    Saved card 12 [green]
    Apple Pay 8
  }

  chart conversion: Checkout conversion [line, unit: %] {
    week | Web | Mobile
    W1   | 61  | 48
    W2   | 63  | 51
    W3   | 66  | 55
    W4   | 70  | 60
  }

  chart tokens: Tokens per AI edit [area, stacked] {
    week | Prompt | Reply
    W1   | 1800   | 300
    W2   | 1500   | 260
    W3   | 1100   | 240
  }

  chart methods: Payment methods [pie, unit: %] {
    Card 62
    Apple Pay 21
    PayPal 12
    Other 5
  }

  chart budget: Budget [donut, unit: k€] {
    Engineering 420
    Design 90
    Infra 60
  }

  chart ideas: Effort vs impact [scatter] {
    idea          | effort | impact
    Saved cards   | 5      | 8
    Apple Pay     | 3      | 9
    One-page      | 8      | 7
    Guest by default | 2   | 4
  }
}
